int status = 1;
int x = 4;
if (status == 1 && x < 4) {
  digitalWrite(LED, HIGH);
}

Apa yang terjadi pada blok if tersebut?

questions.question_en:
Look at the following code:

int status = 1;
int x = 4;
if (status == 1 && x < 4) {
  digitalWrite(LED, HIGH);
}

What happens to that if block?

questions.question:
Siswa menulis kode berikut untuk menginisialisasi 4 LED:

const int LED[4] = {12, 11, 10, 9};
void setup() {
  for (int i = 0; i <= 4; i++) {
    pinMode(LED[i], OUTPUT);
  }
}

Apa masalah utama pada kode tersebut?

questions.question_en:
A student writes the following code to initialize 4 LEDs:

const int LED[4] = {12, 11, 10, 9};
void setup() {
  for (int i = 0; i <= 4; i++) {
    pinMode(LED[i], OUTPUT);
  }
}

What is the main problem in this code?

questions.question:
Siswa membuat program kecepatan kedip LED dengan push button:

int status = digitalRead(2);
if (status = 1) {
  delay(100);
} else {
  delay(500);
}

LED selalu berkedip cepat meskipun tombol tidak ditekan. Apa penyebabnya?

questions.question_en:
A student makes an LED blink-speed program with a push button:

int status = digitalRead(2);
if (status = 1) {
  delay(100);
} else {
  delay(500);
}

The LED always blinks fast even when the button is not pressed. What is the cause?

